        "difficulty": "medium",
        "question": "<p><strong>Inclined Planes Drill #13:</strong> A mass $m$ is released from rest on an inclined plane of angle $\\theta = 30^\\circ$ with friction coefficient $\\mu_k = 0.20$. Find the time taken to slide a distance $d = 10\\text{ m}$ down the incline ($g = 10\\text{ m/s}^2$).</p>",
        "isFRQ": true,
        "rubric": "<p>Acceleration $a = g(\\sin 30^\\circ - 0.20\\cos 30^\\circ) = 10(0.50 - 0.1732) = 3.27\\text{ m/s}^2$. Time $t = \\sqrt{2d/a} = \\sqrt{20/3.27} \\approx 2.47\\text{ s}$.</p>",
        "options": [
          "Submit analytical derivation in workspace."
        ],
        "answer": "FRQ_MANUAL_EVALUATION",
        "explanation": "<p>$a = 3.27\\text{ m/s}^2$, $t = 2.47\\text{ s}$.</p>"
