        "topic": "Motion Graphs",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "question": "<p><strong>Motion Graphs Drill #13:</strong> An object moves with velocity $v(t) = 4t - t^2\\text{ m/s}$ from $t = 0$ to $t = 4\\text{ s}$. Find the total distance traveled and average velocity.</p>",
        "isFRQ": true,
        "rubric": "<p>Velocity is non-negative for $0 \\le t \\le 4$, so displacement equals distance: $\\Delta x = \\int_0^4 (4t - t^2)\\,dt = [2t^2 - t^3/3]_0^4 = 32 - 64/3 = 32/3 = 10.67\\text{ m}$. Average velocity $v_{\\text{avg}} = \\frac{10.67}{4} = 2.67\\text{ m/s}$.</p>",
        "options": [
          "Submit analytical derivation in workspace."
        ],
        "answer": "FRQ_MANUAL_EVALUATION",
        "explanation": "<p>$\\Delta x = 10.67\\text{ m}$, $v_{\\text{avg}} = 2.67\\text{ m/s}$.</p>"
